## Verified Benchmark & Stability Results

Measured with the `diag` build profile on **RTX 5060 Laptop (8 GB VRAM)**, **16 GB RAM**, **Windows 11 x64**, **`series-s` default target (`1920×1080`)**:

| Run / Wave | Mean FPS | Median FPS | P95 FPS | Max FPS | Peak Private RAM | Stability (`TDR` / `Device Removed`) |
| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | --- |
| **Wave 5 Final (`fx_v2_w5_final`)** | **15.81** | **22.90** | **29.00** | **30.80** | 15,757 MB (15.39 GB) | **0 TDR / 0 Device Removed** |
| Wave 4B Clean (`fx_v2_w4b_fast2`) | 13.43 | 14.00 | 30.00 | 30.00 | 14,843 MB (14.50 GB) | 0 TDR / 0 Device Removed |
| Wave 4A Skin Fix (`fx_v2_w4a_skin5`) | 16.19 | 20.85 | 29.30 | 30.10 | 14,400 MB (14.06 GB) | 0 TDR / 0 Device Removed |

### Key Wave 4–6 Fixes Included
- **Smooth Async Intro & Busy Cursor Fix (`WM_SETCURSOR`):** Intercepts `WM_SETCURSOR` (`HTCLIENT`) in `victory-hle` so Windows sets `IDC_ARROW` instead of leaving a stuck busy spinner (and hides cleanly during captured 360° mouse-look). Restores `VICTORY_SHADER_LOOP_LIMIT=4096` (warm disk shader cache hits: `2,272/2,272`), `VICTORY_ASYNC_SUBMIT=1`, `VICTORY_ASYNC_PRESENT=1`, `VICTORY_QUEUE2=1`, `VICTORY_HEAP_TEXTURE_MB=8` / `_MS=2`, and `VICTORY_PIPELINE_WAIT_MS=16` (`122s` world entry in `fx_v2_w6_intro_fix` vs `176s`, `30.0 fps / 33.3 ms` warm intro, `0` TDR).
- **Texture & Skin Realism (`Layout::reach` + tight `over_cap` tiers):** Correct subresource detiling reach and adaptive VRAM mip trimming eliminate dark/black character skin artifacts on 8 GB cards.
- **Wave32 Scanline Elimination:** Reverted the `value_uniform` pass (`fe3aa3f0`) that caused horizontal striped artifacts across characters and lighting on NVIDIA wave32 GPUs.
- **Locked Default Preset (`apply_runtime_defaults()`):** Automatically configured for both `gta6` (1-click launcher) and `victory run --execute` (`series-s` default):
  - `VICTORY_CARD_BUFFERS_MB=1280`, `VICTORY_GPU_UPLOAD_MB=768`
  - `VICTORY_ASYNC_SUBMIT=1`, `VICTORY_ASYNC_PRESENT=1`, `VICTORY_QUEUE2=1` (`VICTORY_INPLACE` and `QUEUE2=6` disabled)
  - `VICTORY_COPY_PLAIN=1`, `VICTORY_PAGE_WRITES=slots`, `VICTORY_TEXTURE_NO_WAIT=1`
  - `VICTORY_JOIN_PARTS=1`, `VICTORY_INDIRECT_GATHER=1`, `VICTORY_HEAP_SYNC=1`, `VICTORY_VIEW_OWN_COPY=1`
  - `VICTORY_HEAP_TEXTURE_MB=8`, `VICTORY_HEAP_TEXTURE_MS=2`, `VICTORY_PIPELINE_WAIT_MS=16`, `VICTORY_SHADER_LOOP_LIMIT=4096`
  - `VICTORY_AMBIENT=0.6`, `VICTORY_AMBIENT_REFLECT=0.5`, `VICTORY_AMBIENT_GI=1`

---

## Build & Run

### 1. Prerequisites
- Windows 11 x64 + D3D12-capable GPU (8 GB+ VRAM, 16 GB+ System RAM recommended)
- Visual Studio 2022/2026 C++ Build Tools (MSVC linker & `rc.exe`)
- Pinned Rust toolchain (configured via `rust-toolchain.toml`, MSRV `1.88.0`)

### 2. Build Release Binaries
```powershell
cargo build --release -p victory --bin gta6 --bin victory
```

### 3. Launch
Place `victory.toml` pointing to your local game dump next to `gta6.exe` (outside the repository), then run:
```powershell
# 1-click launcher (defaults to Xbox Series S + tuned preset)
.\target\release\gta6.exe

# Or explicit CLI launch
.\target\release\victory.exe run --execute --console series-s <path-to-game-executable>
```

> **Release Smoke Test:** Verified 25s zero-argument startup of `gta6.exe` (`~6,606 MB` Private RAM, `0` missing imports, `0` panics).

